WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.954
Under the soil, the land is made of rock.

2
00:00:07.174 --> 00:00:10.518
There are many kinds of rock.
People dig it out and use it.

3
00:00:11.018 --> 00:00:14.780
Granite is very hard. It has
speckles of different colours.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.900
Chalk is soft and white. It
crumbles, and you can write with it.

5
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.325
Sandstone is grainy,
like sand stuck together.

6
00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:25.285
Marble is smooth and shiny when polished.

7
00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:29.313
Slate is dark. It splits
into thin flat sheets.

8
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:33.991
Pumice is full of holes. It is
so light that it floats on water.

9
00:00:34.211 --> 00:00:37.648
Not all rock is grey and hard.
Not all rock is the same.

10
00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:42.374
Test a rock to find its properties.
A property is what it is like.

11
00:00:42.594 --> 00:00:47.052
Scratch it with a coin. Chalk
scratches, but granite is too hard.

12
00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:50.848
Drop water on it. Does the
water soak in, or run off?

13
00:00:51.068 --> 00:00:54.922
Chalk and sandstone soak it
up. Granite and marble do not.

14
00:00:55.142 --> 00:00:59.647
Look with a hand lens. Is it
grainy, smooth, or full of holes?

15
00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:03.536
Every rock has its own
properties. Testing finds them.

16
00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:07.797
Rock is not made in a factory.
It is dug out of the Earth.

17
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:13.265
A quarry is a huge open pit. Rock
is cut and blasted out in blocks.

18
00:01:13.485 --> 00:01:18.872
A mine is tunnels deep underground.
Miners with lamps dig the rock out.

19
00:01:19.092 --> 00:01:22.575
A riverbed is where water
has worn rock into pebbles.

20
00:01:22.795 --> 00:01:25.581
The smooth pebbles and
gravel are scooped out.

21
00:01:26.081 --> 00:01:29.100
Look around you. Rock is
everywhere, doing jobs.

22
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:33.267
Slate on roofs. Stone in
walls. Gravel on paths.

23
00:01:33.487 --> 00:01:35.995
Marble on floors, and chalk on the board.

24
00:01:36.215 --> 00:01:39.234
All of it began in a
quarry, a mine or a river.

25
00:01:39.454 --> 00:01:42.147
But a brick is not rock.
People make bricks.

26
00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:48.127
The environment is everything around
us: land, water, air and living things.

27
00:01:48.347 --> 00:01:52.945
Dumping rubbish in a river, smoke,
concrete on a meadow: these harm.

28
00:01:53.165 --> 00:01:57.577
Planting trees, recycling,
keeping streams clean: these help.

29
00:01:57.797 --> 00:02:02.673
A quarry is not only bad. An old
one can become a lake for wildlife.

30
00:02:02.893 --> 00:02:07.305
Ask: is the land, water or air
better or worse after this?

31
00:02:07.805 --> 00:02:11.845
Rocks are not all the same.
Testing finds their properties.

32
00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:16.477
Rock is taken from quarries, mines
and riverbeds. We use it everywhere.

33
00:02:16.697 --> 00:02:21.016
What we do changes the Earth. It
can help the land, or harm it.
